{#- uid/gid pinned to the `healthchecks` system account (pillar/healthchecks.sls):
   the image runs as its own `hc` user (no fixed uid); the container runs as
   this account instead (Podman `User=`, mapped 1:1), so the SQLite DB in
   data_dir stays owned by it on the host. The matching formulas/users
   account entry must use the same numbers.

   site_root: the URL the UI and ping URLs are built from; its host part is
   what Django accepts (allowed_hosts adds localhost for the image's own
   HEALTHCHECK, which queries 127.0.0.1).

   secret_key: Django's SECRET_KEY (sessions, signed links) — empty here on
   purpose, pillar fills it from OpenBao; empty or unresolved fails
   config.sls (Healthchecks never starts without it).

   env: plain settings for the container (Healthchecks reads its whole config
   from the environment, docs "Server configuration"). Merged with pillar's
   lookup:env key by key. Registration off, no SMTP (no mail integration, no
   password reset — the superuser logs in with its password), private IPs
   allowed for integrations (ntfy on this LAN), 2 gunicorn workers instead
   of the image's 4 (RAM budget, capacity.md).

   api_key (secret-scan: allow): project API key (read-write) for provision.sls — optional. It only
   exists after the first login (created in the UI), so a missing one skips
   provisioning instead of failing; pings auto-create their checks anyway.
   checks: what provision.sls upserts via the Management API (unique by
   slug, all integrations assigned): slug, name, and timeout+grace (seconds)
   or schedule+tz+grace, optional tags/desc. Checks removed from the list are
   not deleted. provision_dir: root-only, holds the API key, the rendered
   check list and the stamp of the last successful run.

   podman: spec overrides for the container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'docker.io/healthchecks/healthchecks',
    'tag': 'v5.0.3',
    'container_name': 'healthchecks',
    'uid': 975,
    'gid': 975,
    'http_port': 8000,
    'base_dir': '/opt/healthchecks',
    'data_dir': '/opt/healthchecks/data',
    'provision_dir': '/opt/healthchecks/provision',
    'provision_script': '/usr/local/sbin/healthchecks-provision',
    'python': '/usr/bin/python3',
    'site_root': '',
    'allowed_hosts': [],
    'secret_key': '',
    'env': {
        'DEBUG': 'False',
        'DB': 'sqlite',
        'DB_NAME': '/data/hc.sqlite',
        'SITE_NAME': 'Homelab Healthchecks',
        'REGISTRATION_OPEN': 'False',
        'EMAIL_USE_VERIFICATION': 'False',
        'INTEGRATIONS_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS': 'True',
        'GUNICORN_WORKERS': '2',
    },
    'api_key': '',
    'checks': [],
    'podman': {},
} %}
{%- set healthchecks = salt['pillar.get']('healthchecks:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
{%- set _key = healthchecks.api_key %}
{%- do healthchecks.update({'provision': (_key is string and _key | length > 0 and not _key.startswith('sdb://'))}) %}
